  },
  {
   "id": "EH2208G",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "✗ **EH2208G** · hypothesis\n\nAitken/geometric extrapolation of fixed-width log ratios predicts new cell log ratio\n\n*why dead:* Ran: prediction error 3.2e-4 of last diff (w35 and w36): consistent but not exact, redundant with EH2208C; dead as an exactness check.",
   "x": 7980,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "1"
  },
  {
   "id": "X4",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "✗ **X4** · tool\n\njob spec with relative cwd started by the launchd ticker\n\n*why dead:* ticker starts in '/', cd failed before logging; fixed: submit stores abspath, tick resolves vs workdir, cd errors go to out.log; preflight warns on missing cwd",
   "x": 8400,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "1"
  },
  {
   "id": "E2213",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**E2213** · experiment\n\npool moved into job queue as ad79-w37-39-pool-q: 2 parallel jobs, POOL_CAP_FACTOR=4.0 (w37 2333 s), after 4-parallel cap-1283 s timeouts under swap contention; old pool PID 25617 + 4 children killed by exact pid",
   "x": 5460,
   "y": 220,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "3"
  },
  {
   "id": "EH2208H",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**EH2208H** · fact\n\nUpdate to EH2208D at 00:12:30: w=37 j=16 also TIMEOUT (4 timeouts j13-16); per-prime runtime rose 290-305s (j0-3) -> 686-877s (j4-11) -> TIMEOUT (j13-16), consistent with host memory/swap pressure; next run should rerun j13-16 with fewer concurrent jobs",
   "x": 7140,
   "y": 220,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "CC2208A",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**CC2208A** · result\n\ncross-check: extender (hs_mod) vs far.py T(w,79-w) exact decimal-string equality w=17..34: 18/18 AGREE, 0 disagree; all far rows pub_mismatch 0 + check prime ok; extender rows 0 mismatches (compare_out.txt)",
   "x": 3360,
   "y": 220,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "4"
  },
  {
   "id": "CC2208B",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**CC2208B** · result\n\nindependence audit: far code imports only sys/os/time/json/resource/numpy/concurrent/datetime, 0 mentions of hs_mod/extender; prime sets per width w=17..34 intersection 0 (far max 1073741789 <2^30, hs min 2147482859 >2^30); far res primes == computed lists; extender value mod all 589 far (w,p) residues: 589 ok 0 bad. Encodings differ in ranking/sweep but share product state shape V(k)xV(w-k)",
   "x": 3780,
   "y": 220,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "4"
  },
  {
   "id": "CC2208C",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**CC2208C** · result\n\nfresh-prime spot check: own dense 2^w bitmask broken-profile counter (trial-division primes 536870909, 268435399; in neither code) passes 882 published cells w<=11 x2 primes 0 mism, negatives novert 1430 / nohoriz 1562 mism; T(w,79-w) mod p for w=17..22 matches BOTH tables 12/12",
   "x": 3780,
   "y": 440,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "4"
  },
  {
   "id": "CC2208D",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "✗ **CC2208D** · hypothesis\n\nown fresh-prime counter at large widths w>=30 via dense 2^w array\n\n*why dead:* 2^30 int64 = 8 GiB per array, far over the 500 MB cap / swap-full host; twin of H1708B; fresh-prime check at w>=23 needs a Fibonacci-frontier counter (own, ~F(w+2) states)",
   "x": 4200,
   "y": 220,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "1"
  },
  {
   "id": "SC2208A",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**SC2208A** · result\n\nsettled-check run 2208: A089980 d=79 NOT published (b-file sha a28e1a8d identical, d<=78; A089934 b-file d<=78 edited 2026-09-22; A006506 n<=39, A028420 n<=27; arXiv 24 mo nothing new; GitHub repos 0, code search 401 PENDING; Zenodo none). No injection",
   "x": 840,
